  "d_dimensional_form": {
   "statement": "delta S^(1) = kappa { sum_(r=G,W) [ A_r O_A^(r,d) + Gamma_r O_g^(r,d) + K_r O_c^(r,d) ] + t_B Q_T^(B,d) + sum_(r=G,W,B) F_r int d^d x (-1/4 Fbar^(r)_(mu nu) Fbar^(r mu nu)) + sum_f (dZ_f/2) O_psi^f + C_H O_H^(d) - Yt int d^d x (Dbar_mu H)^dag Dbar^mu H + Y4 Q_lambda + X_lambda^bos Q_lambda + X_m^bos Q_m + sum_k dy_k^bos Q^+_(y_k) + sum_r c_EA^(r) E_A^(r) + c_EH E_H }, with O^(d) the directions of eq:closed continued with unsplit d-dimensional indices, fields and derivatives; fermion bilinears (Q_K, Q_V, Q_R, Yukawa) have a unique continuation (P_cbar gamma^mu P_c = gbar^mu P_c).",
   "coefficients": {
    "A_G (O_A^(d))": "5*g_s**2/2",
